From d89dc4ae37046db4396f3fc426ed7bf7a780f23d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "github-actions[bot]" <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 12:54:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs: scope histogram delta-temporality limitation to
 collector ES exporter

Both delta and cumulative temporality are now supported for histograms
and counters via the Elasticsearch OTLP endpoint (motlp) on stack 9.5+
and serverless. The delta-only restriction still applies to the
collector's Elasticsearch exporter.

Related to #648

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md b/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md
index 83c913a..e75adef 100644
--- a/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md
+++ b/docs/reference/compatibility/limitations.md
@@ -58,11 +58,16 @@ When collecting host metrics through a distribution of the OTel Collector other
 
 ## Metrics data ingestion
 
-### Histograms in delta temporality only
+### Histogram and counter temporality
 
-Ingestion of OpenTelemetry metrics with the type [`Histogram`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#histogram) are only supported with [`delta temporality`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#temporality). Histograms with `cumulative` temporality are dropped before being ingested into {{es}}.
+```{applies_to}
+stack: ga 9.5
+serverless: ga
+```
 
-Make sure to export histogram metrics with delta temporality or use the [`cumulativetodelta processor`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/processor/cumulativetodeltaprocessor) as a workaround to convert the temporality for histogram metrics.
+When you send data using the [{{es}} OTLP endpoint](docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality) (`motlp`), both `delta` and `cumulative` [temporality](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#temporality) are supported for histograms and counters. Refer to [Metric temporality](docs-content://manage-data/ingest/otlp-endpoint.md#metric-temporality) for details, including the requirement to set `xpack.otel_data.histogram_field_type` to `exponential_histogram` for cumulative histograms. This setting is the default from stack version 9.4.
+
+When you send data through the collector's {{es}} exporter, ingestion of OpenTelemetry metrics with the type [`Histogram`](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otel/metrics/data-model/#histogram) is only supported with `delta` temporality. Histograms with `cumulative` temporality are dropped before being ingested into {{es}}. This restriction doesn't apply to counters. Make sure to export histogram metrics with delta temporality or use the [`cumulativetodelta processor`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/processor/cumulativetodeltaprocessor) as a workaround to convert the temporality for histogram metrics.
 
 ### Exemplars
 
